    "final_answer": "Based on the `config/lamp.toml` file, the lamp range is set to **18 nm** (nanometers).\n\nThis refers to a wavelength of 18 nanometers, which falls in the **extreme ultraviolet (EUV)** or soft X-ray region of the electromagnetic spectrum. This is an extremely short wavelength, typically used in specialized applications like:\n- EUV lithography for semiconductor manufacturing\n- Scientific research instruments\n- Specialized plasma sources\n\nNote that 18 nm is not a typical range for common lighting lamps (which usually operate in visible light at 400-700 nm or UV-A at around 365 nm). This appears to be a specialized EUV source configuration."
